   - If \( s > 1 \), \( A > 1 \), and the \( e.e \) of the product is higher than the starting material, indicating amplification of the enantiomeric excess.  
   - The amplification factor \( A \) increases with \( s \).  
   - For \( s \gg 1 \), the \( e.e \) of the product approaches \( 0 \) (e.e = 0), indicating a highly enriched homochiral product.  

