\[
\frac{1}{L_m} = \frac{1}{L_1} + \frac{1}{L_2}
\]  
where \( L_m \) is the flillability limit of the mixture, \( L_1 \) and \( L_2 \) are the flillacity limits of the two components, respectively.  

This equation is derived from the **Dalley's equation**, which relates the flillability limits of a mixture to the flillinities of its components.  

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
