   For an ideal gas, the meanolecular Gibbs free energy (\(\mu\)) is:
   \[
   \mu = -kT \ln(p)
   \]
   Thus, the free Helmholtz factor is:
   \[
   \exp(\mu/kT) = \exp\left(\frac{-kT \ln(p)}{kT}\right) = \exp\left(-\ln(p)\right) = \frac{1}{p}
   \]
   Given \(p = 1 \, \text{bar} = 10^5 \, \text{Pa}\):
