   - Substituting the values:
     \[
     E = \frac{1}{2} \times 1.0 \times 10^6 \, \text{Pa} \times 0.001 \, \text{m}^3 = 500 \, \text{J}
     \]
   - The energy in the pressure wave is 70% of the total energy:
     \[
     \text{Energy in pressure wave} = 0.7 \times 500 \, \text{J} = 350 \, \text{J}
     \]

