","The entropy production rate \( \pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{d\Omega}{dt} = \frac{d\eta}{dT} \ln \left( \frac{d\eta}{dT} \right) + \ln \left( \frac{d\eta}{dT} \right)
\]
where \( \Delta S = \eta \ln \left( \frac{d\eta}{dT} \right) \), and \( \Delta S = \frac{dQ}{T} \).

For the sliding of two surfaces, the work done by the friction force is:
\[
W = \frac{1}{2} F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
This work is converted into heat, and the entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{Q}{T} = \frac{W}{T} = \frac{1}{2} \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\pi_S = \frac{1}{2} \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
