- **Thermal conductivity**: The key factor is thermal conductivity. High thermal conductivity means heat can easily pass through the material. Glass is a poor conductor, with a thermal conductivity of around 100 W/m²K. This is much lower than traditional heat-conducting materials like glass-based glasses (1000 W/m²K) or glass-based glasses (1000 W/m²K).

