2. Surface modification: Plasma treatment can be used to modify the surface properties of the silicon or other materials in the solar cell, such as hydrophobicity, roughness, and surface charge. This can help to improve the performance of the solar cell by reducing surface defects, improving the adhesion of thin-thin films, and enhancing the overall performance of the solar cell.

