4. Nanostructured structures: Plasma can be used to create nanostructures on the surface of the solar cell, such as nanowires, nanowires, and nanowires. These nanostructures can enhance the absorption of sunlight, improve the charge transport properties, and enhance the overall performance of the solar cell.

5. Thin film fabrication: Plasma can be used to form thin films with high thickness and thickness control, which can be used as a protective layer or as an additional active material in the solar cell. This can help to improve the performance of the solar cell by reducing surface defects, improving the adhesion of thin films, and enhancing the overall performance of the solar cell.

