\[
\Delta E \cdot \tau = \hbar /2
\]
where \(\hbar\) is the reduced Planck constant (\(\hbar = frac{h}{2\pi} \approx 1.00 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}\)).

First, we need to convert the lifetime from seconds to meters per second (since the energy is given in MeV, we will need to convert the energy to joules for consistency with \(\hbar\)):
\[
